WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.680
Even the power of all six Infinity Stones
combined has its limits.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.100
So declared Avengers: Endgame screenwriters
Christopher Markus and Stephen McFeely in

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.870
a recent sitdown with the New York Times,
addressing the heart-wrenching death of one

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.540
of the MCU's longest-tenured characters.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.720
Fair warning: we’ll be discussing spoilers
from here on.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.980
On a quest to the past to recover the Soul
Stone from the planet Vormir before it was

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.789
acquired by Thanos, Clint Barton and Natasha
Romanoff find themselves faced with the same

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:30.920
conundrum as the Mad Titan in Avengers: Infinity
War.

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.460
To possess the stone, you must lose that which
you love.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:39.020
In a heartbreaking illustration of the pair's
bond, they end up actually fighting each other,

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.760
each determined to be the one to go over the
cliff to their deaths so that the other can

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:43.860
complete the mission.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:48.920
In the end, the Black Widow prevails and plunges
to her doom on the planet's rocky beach, leaving

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.650
a distraught Hawkeye wailing to the heavens
with the glowing stone in hand.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:56.620
The Times asked Markus and McFeely: Why did
Black Widow have to die?

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:01.260
Bruce Banner used the power of the Tony Stark-built
Infinity Gauntlet to bring back all of the

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.860
heroes who perished in Infinity War's Decimation.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.260
Why could he not bring her back, as well?

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:11.540
"This is monsters and magic and nothing we
were ever trained for."

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.920
The writers offered a little insight into
their thought process in dealing with the

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:18.440
death of a founding Avenger, the only woman
on the original team.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.660
McFeely says:

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:38.100
But do the other characters and the audience
get a chance to mourn such a central character?

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.920
McFeely says that was a huge challenge for
the writing duo.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.040
Markus adds:

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:04.360
The answer lies in the very nature of the
Soul Stone, and the trade that it demands.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:08.540
McFeely makes it clear that bringing back
Natasha would mean giving up the stone.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:13.670
Apparently, if Banner had concentrated with
single-minded focus on resurrecting Romanoff,

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:18.840
he may have sealed the fate of literally everyone
else by giving up the Soul Stone, negating

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.820
the noble sacrifice she had made.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:26.180
The writers also revealed that an early version
of the script had Hawkeye, not Black Widow,

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:30.140
making the sacrifice, but the impassioned
plea of a member of Endgame's crew changed

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:30.980
their minds.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:31.960
McFeely said,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.540
"We're still friends, right?"

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.050
"Depends on how hard you hit me."

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:48.840
In the MCU's timeline, Earth's Mightiest Heroes
will be Black Widow-less going forward.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.500
But that won't stop Mighty Marvel from looking
into the past: after being promised for years,

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:57.630
Black Widow is finally getting her own solo
film, which is currently in production and

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:01.580
will focus on the future Avenger's early years
and recruitment by S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:06.160
The film's official synopsis reveals that
the flick will take place 15 years after the

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:11.100
fall of the Soviet Union, which would put
it right around 2006, before the Iron Man

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:13.890
armor was even a gleam in Tony Stark's eye.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:19.200
Johansson will reprise her role, and the flick
also boasts the red-hot Florence Pugh, David

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.600
Harbour, and Rachel Weisz among its cast.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.380
Aussie director Cate Shortland is set to helm
the picture from a script by Jac Schaeffer,

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:30.640
who contributed to the screenplay for Captain
Marvel and will run the Vision and Scarlet

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.780
Witch limited series for Disney-Plus.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:37.080
So, while the only true family she's ever
known may have seen the last of Romanoff,

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.390
the viewing audience has not.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:44.920
Black Widow is expected to be the first film
of the MCU's Phase 4, which raises another

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:49.819
intriguing question: how will its events figure
into whatever grand, overarching narrative

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.820
Marvel Studios has planned next?

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:56.380
We can't wait to find out, and to see Scarlett
Johansson suit up as our favorite Russian

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.300
superspy at least one more time.

